<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Mexico</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Santa Fe de Nuevo México</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> is a region of the south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, today a US state. Spanish colonisation began under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-onate">Juan de Oñate</a> in 1598, and the province, centred on Santa Fe from about 1610, was the northern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pueblo-revolt">Pueblo Revolt</a> of 1680 drove the Spaniards out until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-vargas">Diego de Vargas</a> returned in 1692. It passed to Mexico in 1821 and to the United States in 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-mexico.jpg" alt="New Mexico" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
